  "current_status_control": "Rechecked 2026-09-05: IMD's press release dated 4 September 2026 observed a fresh Western Disturbance as a middle- and upper-tropospheric trough roughly along 64°E north of 32°N. Its rainfall outlook was explicitly issued under several simultaneous synoptic systems, so no realised or forecast rainfall is attributed to the disturbance alone. The package teaches the static jet/Rossby-wave/western-disturbance mechanism while keeping observation, nowcast, forecast, warning, impact and climatology separate; one dated trough does not establish a long-term jet trend.",
